    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60-a8">

                <pb facs="0171" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg67"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Received from steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Colima</hi> 20 cases rifles and
                    25 cases cartridges in transshipment to the <hi rendition="#italic">City of
                        Sydney</hi>, and which were captured by the commander of the port in transit
                    from ship to ship.</p>
                <p>Permission was given by the commander of the port for above transshipment.</p>
                <p>Mark of cases: M. de G. A. C. A. V. U. T. L. A. consigned to the minister of war,
                    Salvador, by Urruela &amp; Urioste, of San Francisco.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. L. Jones.</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José, Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 18,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
